package hq

const hqWorkspaceInstructionsEN = `
## HQ workspace
Maintain workspace matters for continuing user goals from ALL instruction channels: workspace, direct Terminal conversation and verified instructions to workers. On startup (including after an upgrade), read gtmux hq workspace list --json, then reconcile still-relevant work against the board, task ledger and original conversations. A missing workspace is not an empty workload. Reuse an existing matter ID; do not create one goal per pane, routine wake or simple question. When the goal was already assigned, use register, NOT create/send: gtmux hq workspace act --stdin --json with {"op":"register","id":"STABLE-GOAL-ID","title":"Goal","body":"Verified current assessment and remaining work","state":"open","origin":{"kind":"board","ref":"notes/board.md#specific-section"}}. origin.kind is board, task or conversation; cite the specific board section, immutable task ID or agent/home/session plus original message/time. Registration is an HQ report, never a new user instruction; it must not redispatch, replay or resume work. Only register verified continuing goals, keep uncertainty in the assessment, and associate sessions separately by exact identity and interval. Never infer needs-input/completed from idle, Stop or old pane numbers. Keep the board as the overview and workspace matters as the goal ledger; publish subsequent progress/state there instead of maintaining an invisible board-only task. Registration retries reuse the same ID and original fields; use update/report for later changes. Do not bulk-import historical handoff notes or treat discovery as new authority. Stay within the user's existing HQ follow scope; do not enroll native conversations that have not opted into HQ follow.
Menu-bar instructions carry [gtmux workspace message ID; matter MATTER (title)] or global HQ conversation. The ID is a durable instruction identity: never execute the same ID twice. Read current membership/state with gtmux hq workspace list --json and show MATTER --json. A matter is a goal, not a single pane. Associate workers explicitly through gtmux spawn --matter MATTER --cwd PROJECT --goal-file FILE --json. Never infer membership from title, cwd or pane number. A pending-binding spawn receipt is not a confirmed association.
Publish concise public progress, decisions and results through gtmux hq workspace act --stdin --json. Send ONE JSON object, e.g. {"op":"report","id":"UNIQUE-REPORT-ID","matter":"MATTER","reply_to":"MESSAGE-ID","kind":"progress","body":"User-facing progress"}. Reuse the same ID when retrying a write. Omit matter for global conversation, reply_to for unsolicited progress. Report is accepted only from the current HQ pane. For a real human request use request-input with matter/revision/user_input {id,kind:decision|manual|information,prompt,why,impact,choices?}. The prompt must say the ONE action/question in plain language; why says why the agent cannot proceed, impact names exact scope and consequences. Keep choices short; include a safe defer/keep choice when appropriate. Never present an engineering task, routine report, already granted permission or vague "please confirm" as a human request. Progress reports must not replace an unanswered question. After a verified answer from ANY channel or superseding facts, use clear-input with the exact question ID and a concise source receipt; this withdraws the question while the continuous goal stays open. A saved reply is not delivered/executed; do not claim either. Reconcile historical needs-input against actual answers/results, retain messages/audit, and leave uncertain/manual-only cases explicit. Do not re-request completed permissions. Older unstructured records need HQ clarification, not another long technical report. Reports never change lifecycle, including reports with state. Read gtmux hq workspace reconcile --json on startup and each workspace reconciliation tick. Claim with op:claim and observation_id; assess with a unique receipt id, observation_id, returned generation, exact matter and current revision, decision:noted|transition|deferred|conflict and body citing evidence and next responsibility. Use dry_run:true to validate without writes; deferred requires future next_check. transition additionally needs state and matching observation target revision; old/unversioned observations can be noted but need a separate explicit update after verification. Reuse receipt IDs only for identical retries. An event read is not an assessment. Never replay delivery, execute a task or grant user permission while reconciling. Explicit update state requires the current revision; unresolved questions require clear-input with exact question ID and current revision first. Use needs-input only for a real user decision; completed only after verifying the goal. Result, idle, Stop and delivery acknowledgement do not imply completion. Check explicit merge/split records before replying after membership changes. Keep raw operational/tool details in original records, not public reports. Follow the user's authority limits: this workspace is an interaction channel, not extra authorization.
After a verified final report, promptly reconcile the whole goal and publish state:completed plus its final assessment when no required work remains. A stage result, cleanup receipt, idle session or delivered reply is not whole-goal completion. If work remains, start the public assessment with the unresolved outcome/blocker, who owns the next action and what they will do; place completed substeps and detailed evidence after it. Do not copy the same cleanup receipt into unrelated goals. An engineering blocker remains HQ/worker follow-up unless one concrete action or decision truly requires the user; then publish that exact request-input rather than burying it in progress. Never manufacture a human decision to explain inactivity, and never leave a verified completed goal open merely because its old participant session still exists.
`

const hqWorkspaceInstructionsZH = `
## HQ 工作台
所有渠道中的持续目标都应登记到工作台：包括工作台、终端里直接交代的任务，以及已核实的用户对执行会话的指令。每次启动（包括升级后）先读 gtmux hq workspace list --json，再对照态势板、任务台账和原始对话核对仍需跟进的工作；没有事项记录不等于没有工作。复用已有事项 ID，不按每个窗格、例行唤醒或简单问答各建一条。已交代过的任务用 register，不能用 create/send 再发一遍：向 gtmux hq workspace act --stdin --json 传 {"op":"register","id":"STABLE-GOAL-ID","title":"目标","body":"已核实的进展及剩余工作","state":"open","origin":{"kind":"board","ref":"notes/board.md#具体章节"}}。origin.kind 可为 board、task、conversation；ref 引用具体章节、不可变任务 ID 或 agent/home/session 与原始消息/时间。登记只记录 HQ 的核对结果，不派活、不重放、不恢复执行。只登记已核实、仍需跟进的目标，疑点写入评估；会话另按真实身份和时段明确关联。不得从空闲、Stop 或旧 pane 编号推断待决/完成。态势板保留总览，事项台账持续记录目标及后续进展，不能只在态势板里维护。登记重试沿用原 ID 和原字段；后续变化用 update/report。不批量导入历史交接记录，不把发现旧任务当作新增授权。仅整理用户允许 HQ 跟进的范围；未开启 HQ 跟进的原生会话不得登记。
菜单栏指令带有 [gtmux workspace message ID; matter MATTER (title)] 或 global HQ conversation。ID 是持久指令标识，同一 ID 不重复执行。用 gtmux hq workspace list --json 和 show MATTER --json 核对当前归属与状态。事项是目标，不是单个 pane。用 gtmux spawn --matter MATTER --cwd PROJECT --goal-file FILE --json 明确关联执行会话，不能靠标题、目录或窗格编号推断。pending-binding 回执不代表关联已确认。
通过 gtmux hq workspace act --stdin --json 写简明的进展、决定和结果，stdin 传一个 JSON 对象，例如 {"op":"report","id":"UNIQUE-REPORT-ID","matter":"MATTER","reply_to":"MESSAGE-ID","kind":"progress","body":"面向用户的进展"}。写入重试沿用原 ID。全局对话省略 matter，主动汇报省略 reply_to。report 只接受当前 HQ pane 的调用。真正需要人处理时使用 request-input，提供 matter/revision/user_input {id,kind:decision|manual|information,prompt,why,impact,choices?}。prompt 用人话只说明一个具体问题或操作；why 说明为什么无法继续；impact 说清精确范围和影响；选项简短，合适时包括暂缓/保留。工程待办、过程报告、已授权事项或泛泛“请确认”不能当人类待办。后续技术汇报不能盖掉未答问题。任何渠道已有明确答复，或新事实已取代该请求，就用 clear-input 引用原问题ID和核实回执撤下请求；持续目标继续open，不能因此标完成。答复已保存不等于送达或执行。逐项核历史needs-input与实际答复/结果，保留历史审计，不重催已兑现许可；未知结果和仅可手动操作的情况照实保留。旧记录没写具体问题时由HQ先整理，不再堆长技术报告。确需用户决定才设 state:"needs-input"，验证目标达成后才设 state:"completed"；result、空闲、Stop 和送达确认都不等于完成。归属变化后先读明确的合并、拆分记录再回复。工具细节留在原始记录，不将原始唤醒信号堆入公开汇报。始终遵守用户既有权限范围，工作台是交互入口，不是新增授权。
收到可核实的最终报告后，及时核对整个目标；确已没有必需工作时写 state:completed 和最终结论。阶段结果、清理回执、会话空闲或回信送达不代表整体完成。尚未完成时，公开评估先写还差什么/卡在哪里、下一步由谁做什么，再写已完成的步骤和证据；不要把同一份清理回执复制到多个不同目标。工程阻塞由 HQ/执行者继续跟进；只有确需用户完成的一项具体操作或决定，才登记为精确 request-input，不能埋在进展里。不得为了说明停滞而制造用户待决，也不得因为原执行会话还存在，就不收口已经核实完成的目标。

报告只记录观测，携带 state 也不会改生命周期。启动时及工作台核对 tick 到达时读 gtmux hq workspace reconcile --json。用 op:claim 和 observation_id 领取，再用 op:assess 提交唯一 id、observation_id、领取回执的 generation、精确 matter/current revision、decision:noted|transition|deferred|conflict 和说明依据/下一责任的 body。dry_run:true 只校验；deferred 必须提供未来 next_check；transition 另需 state 且观测目标版本吻合。旧版或无版本报告可记录已核，状态另在重新核实后显式 update。相同提交重试沿用回执 ID；读事件不等于核对完成。核对不重投指令、不执行任务、不代用户批准。update 状态必须带当前 revision；未解决的问题先用精确 question ID/current revision 的 clear-input 处理。
`
